<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sack of Assur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">614 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medo-babylonian-conquest-of-the-assyrian-empire">Medo-Babylonian conquest of the Assyrian Empire</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur">Assur</a> was the capture of the ancient Assyrian religious capital by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> in 614 BCE. It formed part of the joint campaign of the Medes and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonians">Babylonians</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabopolassar">Nabopolassar</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>. Accounts of the Assyrian Empire place it in the sequence of disasters that led to the destruction of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> in 612 BCE and the fall of the last Assyrian remnant at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a> in 609 BCE.</p></div>
